# Dual GitHub accounts for homepage work

Alex uses two GitHub destinations for home6 / HubSpot homepage files.

## 1. Automatic — `amacbbn86` (default)

- Repo: https://github.com/amacbbn86/FUNDVIEW_Home (`origin` in this workspace)
- After meaningful homepage edits: **commit and push to `origin/main` automatically** (same standing authorization as the main push rule).
- This is the day-to-day / end-of-day sync source of truth for office pulls.

## 2. On request only — `amcintyre86`

- Repo: https://github.com/amcintyre86/SITE_Home-Page
- Local clone (when present): `C:\Users\amcintyre\Projects\SITE_Home-Page`
- Upload **only** when Alex explicitly asks (e.g. “upload to SITE_Home-Page”, “send to amcintyre86”, “sync the other account”).
- When asked, copy/update at least `home6.html`, `Home6.hubspot.html`, `fundview-header-local.html`, and `fundview-footer-local.html` (regenerate HubSpot export first if needed), commit, and push to that repo’s `main`.
- **Never** push to `amcintyre86/SITE_Home-Page` as part of routine homepage edits.

## Auth note

Pushes to `SITE_Home-Page` require credentials for **amcintyre86**, not the `amacbbn86` token used for `FUNDVIEW_Home`. If push returns 403, stop and tell Alex authentication for `amcintyre86` is needed.
